CH = dict(num=13, tag="Maths", title="Statistics", theme="Mean, median and mode of grouped data",
intro="A school wants to know the typical marks of its Class 10, a doctor the usual pulse rate of patients and a factory the usual lifetime of a bulb. When the data are collected into class intervals, a single representative value, a measure of central tendency, summarises them. This chapter finds the mean, median and mode of grouped data and relates the three.",
big_questions=["How do we find the mean of data given in class intervals?", "How are median and modal class located and the values calculated?", "How are mean, median and mode connected?"],
blocks=[
("h2", "13.1 Mean of Grouped Data"),
("note", "DEFINITION", "In a frequency distribution, each class is represented by its **class mark** x<sub>i</sub> = (upper limit + lower limit)/2. The **mean** is the sum of f<sub>i</sub>x<sub>i</sub> divided by the sum of the frequencies."),
("note", "FORMULA", "**Direct method:** mean = &Sigma;f<sub>i</sub>x<sub>i</sub> / &Sigma;f<sub>i</sub>.  **Assumed mean method:** mean = a + &Sigma;f<sub>i</sub>d<sub>i</sub> / &Sigma;f<sub>i</sub>, where a is an assumed mean (usually the class mark near the middle) and **d<sub>i</sub> = x<sub>i</sub> &minus; a**."),
("table", ["Class", "f<sub>i</sub>", "Class mark x<sub>i</sub>", "f<sub>i</sub>x<sub>i</sub>", "d<sub>i</sub> (a = 35)", "f<sub>i</sub>d<sub>i</sub>"], [["10&ndash;20", "5", "15", "75", "&minus;20", "&minus;100"], ["20&ndash;30", "8", "25", "200", "&minus;10", "&minus;80"], ["30&ndash;40", "12", "35", "420", "0", "0"], ["40&ndash;50", "10", "45", "450", "10", "100"], ["50&ndash;60", "5", "55", "275", "20", "100"], ["**Total**", "**40**", "", "**1420**", "", "**20**"]]),
("p", "**Direct method:** mean = 1420/40 = **35.5**. **Assumed mean method:** mean = 35 + 20/40 = **35.5**. Both methods agree; the second keeps the numbers small."),
("h2", "13.2 Mode of Grouped Data"),
("note", "FORMULA", "The **modal class** is the class with the **highest frequency**.  **Mode = l + [ (f<sub>1</sub> &minus; f<sub>0</sub>) / (2f<sub>1</sub> &minus; f<sub>0</sub> &minus; f<sub>2</sub>) ] x h**, where l = lower limit of the modal class, h = class size, f<sub>1</sub> = frequency of the modal class, f<sub>0</sub> = frequency of the class before it, f<sub>2</sub> = frequency of the class after it."),
("p", "**From the table above:** modal class 30&ndash;40, l = 30, h = 10, f<sub>1</sub> = 12, f<sub>0</sub> = 8, f<sub>2</sub> = 10: mode = 30 + (4/(24 &minus; 18)) x 10 = 30 + 6.67 = **36.67**."),
("h2", "13.3 Median of Grouped Data"),
("steps", [("Step 1 — Make a cumulative frequency (cf) column", "Add frequencies progressively; the last cf equals n."), ("Step 2 — Find n/2 and the median class", "The median class is the class whose cumulative frequency is **just greater than or equal to n/2**."), ("Step 3 — Apply the formula", "Use l, cf, f and h for the median class.")]),
("note", "FORMULA", "**Median = l + [ (n/2 &minus; cf) / f ] x h**, where l = lower limit of the median class, n = total frequency, cf = cumulative frequency of the class **before** the median class, f = frequency of the median class, h = class size."),
("table", ["Class", "f", "cf"], [["10&ndash;20", "5", "5"], ["20&ndash;30", "8", "13"], ["30&ndash;40", "12", "25"], ["40&ndash;50", "10", "35"], ["50&ndash;60", "5", "40"]]),
("p", "Here n = 40, n/2 = 20, so the median class is 30&ndash;40 (cf = 25 &ge; 20). l = 30, cf (before) = 13, f = 12, h = 10: median = 30 + (7/12) x 10 = **35.83**."),
("h2", "13.4 Relationship between the Three"),
("note", "FORMULA", "**3 Median = Mode + 2 Mean**  (an empirical relation for moderately skewed data).  Check: 3 x 35.83 = 107.5 and 36.67 + 2 x 35.5 = 107.67, which are nearly equal."),
("table", ["Measure", "Meaning", "Use"], [["Mean", "The average of all observations", "Marks, wages, when no extreme values"], ["Median", "The middle value; half the observations lie below it", "Income, where a few values are very large"], ["Mode", "The most frequent value", "Most common shoe size, most popular item"]]),
("h2", "13.5 Worked Examples"),
("p", "**Missing frequency.** Classes 0&ndash;10, 10&ndash;20, 20&ndash;30 have frequencies 4, x and 6 and the mean is 16. Class marks are 5, 15, 25, so (20 + 15x + 150)/(10 + x) = 16, giving 170 + 15x = 160 + 16x and **x = 10**."),
("p", "**Finding the mode.** Classes 0&ndash;20, 20&ndash;40, 40&ndash;60, 60&ndash;80 with frequencies 4, 10, 6, 5: modal class 20&ndash;40; mode = 20 + (6/(20 &minus; 4 &minus; 6)) x 20 = 20 + 12 = **32**."),
("p", "**Finding the median.** Frequencies 3, 7, 12, 10, 8 (n = 40) for classes of width 10 starting at 0: cf = 3, 10, 22, 32, 40; n/2 = 20, median class 20&ndash;30; median = 20 + (20 &minus; 10)/12 x 10 = **28.33**."),
("note", "IMPORTANT", "Classes must be **continuous (exclusive)** for the formulae; if the classes are written 10&ndash;19, 20&ndash;29 convert them first. The classes must also have the same width for the mode formula."),
("h2", "Quick Revision: Likely Exam Questions"),
("qa", [("What is a class mark?", "The mid-value of a class: (upper + lower)/2."), ("Write the formula of the mean by the assumed mean method.", "a + &Sigma;f<sub>i</sub>d<sub>i</sub> / &Sigma;f<sub>i</sub>."), ("What is the modal class?", "The class with the highest frequency."), ("How do you find the median class?", "Locate n/2 in the cumulative frequency column."), ("If mean = 12 and median = 11.5, estimate the mode.", "3(11.5) &minus; 2(12) = 10.5."), ("What does cf mean in the median formula?", "Cumulative frequency of the class preceding the median class."), ("When is median preferred?", "When the data have extreme values."), ("Find the class mark of 25&ndash;35.", "30.")]),
],
takeaways=["Mean = **&Sigma;fx/&Sigma;f**, or **a + &Sigma;fd/&Sigma;f**.", "Mode = **l + (f<sub>1</sub> &minus; f<sub>0</sub>)/(2f<sub>1</sub> &minus; f<sub>0</sub> &minus; f<sub>2</sub>) x h**.", "Median = **l + (n/2 &minus; cf)/f x h**.", "**3 Median = Mode + 2 Mean.**"])
